1
00:00:00,038 --> 00:00:01,530
Right now, Praew…

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:02,737
She’s in danger.

3
00:00:03,723 --> 00:00:04,396
Praew!

4
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:06,450
She might be experiencing dissociation.

5
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,977
Even when she wakes up,
she might not remember some moments.

6
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:12,230
I looked through
the information of all four victims.

7
00:00:12,262 --> 00:00:15,530
Their names are all
in the Thai Investment Bank case file

8
00:00:15,610 --> 00:00:16,610
from 20 years ago.

9
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:18,777
You’re still the prime suspect.

10
00:00:18,979 --> 00:00:20,857
(I’ve got all the chapters of Nekros.)

11
00:00:20,902 --> 00:00:23,300
(Is it possible to meet you just once?)

12
00:00:23,331 --> 00:00:25,292
(I’ll give you all the chapters.)

13
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:26,899
Mr. Thun.

14
00:00:27,296 --> 00:00:27,985
Yes.

15
00:00:28,659 --> 00:00:29,417
It’s me.

16
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:34,385
I’ll just be out with it…

17
00:00:34,976 --> 00:00:37,651
I’m a big fan of Mr. Kill.

18
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:40,201
Thank you.

19
00:00:40,883 --> 00:00:43,850
So you have all chapters of Nekros.

20
00:00:44,630 --> 00:00:45,264
Yes.

21
00:00:45,321 --> 00:00:46,222
I do.

22
00:00:46,523 --> 00:00:49,216
And I’m more than willing
to give them all to you,

23
00:00:51,179 --> 00:00:57,198
in exchange for an interview
as the creator of Nekros, though.

24
00:01:02,272 --> 00:01:03,251
Okay, okay, okay.

25
00:01:03,297 --> 00:01:04,302
I get it.

26
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,904
I’m asking for too much.

27
00:01:07,427 --> 00:01:10,899
I know if you wanted to reveal yourself,
you would already have.

28
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,499
And I believe you have a good reason

29
00:01:15,296 --> 00:01:16,570
for keeping your identity hidden.

30
00:01:19,313 --> 00:01:21,697
But I want you to keep in mind

31
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:24,596
you won’t probably find
all chapters of Nekros again.

32
00:01:25,984 --> 00:01:30,102
Do you think a fan like Asura
would keep them?

33
00:01:33,236 --> 00:01:35,210
How’d you know about that?

34
00:01:36,025 --> 00:01:37,859
Praew told me all about it.

35
00:01:38,489 --> 00:01:41,939
She said there was a mysterious fan
sending you information for your manga.

36
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:47,290
I got so excited when I first heard it
and I was reminded of something.

37
00:01:47,971 --> 00:01:50,795
Asura, in Japanese, means titans.

38
00:01:52,673 --> 00:01:57,697
Titan, spelled in English, is Y-A-K.

39
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:03,140
When you think about it,
that’s K-A-Y backwards.

40
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:05,601
Isn’t that your name?

41
00:02:09,052 --> 00:02:13,204
Maybe Asura is something you’ve created,

42
00:02:14,233 --> 00:02:16,699
like a shadow following you.

43
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:19,254
You’re just never aware of it.

44
00:02:24,537 --> 00:02:26,460
I have to go.

45
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:07,500
Maybe Asura is a shadow following you.

46
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,100
You’re just never aware of it.

47
00:04:51,820 --> 00:04:53,800
(Do you still smell smoke, Kaye?)

48
00:04:59,057 --> 00:05:00,142
Who are you?

49
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,601
The fire has gone out,

50
00:05:03,484 --> 00:05:04,902
but the smell of smoke

51
00:05:05,566 --> 00:05:08,099
and the burn on your skin
last longer, don’t they?

52
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:11,203
The most torturing part

53
00:05:12,043 --> 00:05:14,300
is waking up to live your life

54
00:05:14,912 --> 00:05:17,200
when you feel like a walking corpse,

55
00:05:18,104 --> 00:05:20,330
forced to live among people,

56
00:05:20,825 --> 00:05:22,299
forced to smile to the world,

57
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:26,985
when no one knows
you have nothing inside but ashes.

58
00:05:30,310 --> 00:05:32,203
That’s the hardest part, isn’t it?

59
00:05:34,051 --> 00:05:35,096
Just admit it.

60
00:05:36,099 --> 00:05:37,100
You’re me.

61
00:05:37,937 --> 00:05:39,050
And I’m you.

62
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:41,896
No, no, no.

63
00:05:43,728 --> 00:05:44,702
You’re not me.

64
00:05:45,958 --> 00:05:47,090
I’m not you.

65
00:05:47,690 --> 00:05:48,998
I don’t want anyone dead.

66
00:05:53,702 --> 00:05:56,497
Nekros was born from your grudge.

67
00:05:58,220 --> 00:05:59,822
You feel satisfied every time

68
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:03,419
knowing all the victims whose death
you caused were in so much pain.

69
00:06:04,265 --> 00:06:05,198
Am I right?

70
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,690
The screams of all those victims

71
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:14,001
sound like your voice calling for justice
you’ve been screaming.

72
00:06:14,670 --> 00:06:16,897
Isn’t that how you feel?

73
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:24,708
No, no. You’re not me.

74
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:25,650
I’m not you.

75
00:06:26,737 --> 00:06:28,099
Just admit it.

76
00:06:28,446 --> 00:06:29,299
No, no.

77
00:06:30,052 --> 00:06:30,902
Stop.

78
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:32,899
No. I’m not you.

79
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,416
I’ll never be you.

80
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:36,770
I know how you feel
because I feel it, too.

81
00:06:36,868 --> 00:06:37,539
Stop talking.

82
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:38,460
Stop talking!

83
00:06:38,497 --> 00:06:39,542
Stop freaking talking!

84
00:06:39,737 --> 00:06:40,939
Shut up!

85
00:06:41,132 --> 00:06:43,222
Shut up, asshole!
What the hell are you laughing at?

86
00:06:43,246 --> 00:06:44,102
Shut up!

87
00:06:44,305 --> 00:06:45,300
I’m not you!

88
00:06:45,321 --> 00:06:46,219
You jerk!

89
00:06:47,110 --> 00:06:47,900
Stop!

90
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:53,200
Listen up, Kaye.

91
00:06:53,985 --> 00:06:55,200
Just let me out.

92
00:06:56,150 --> 00:06:57,900
The world needs Nekros.

93
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,200
It needs us.

94
00:06:59,728 --> 00:07:02,196
It needs someone
to get rid of those jerks,

95
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,290
those scumbags.

96
00:07:05,198 --> 00:07:06,414
Just admit it, Kaye.

97
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:09,132
You feel just as satisfied as I do.

98
00:07:10,540 --> 00:07:11,499
You’re me.

99
00:07:11,904 --> 00:07:13,004
I’m you.

100
00:07:15,265 --> 00:07:16,700
No one gets you like I do.

101
00:07:23,902 --> 00:07:25,097
Am I right, Kaye?

102
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:07,690
PIMMA LIMKUNCHORN

103
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:15,304
Her condition is still troubling.

104
00:10:15,697 --> 00:10:17,801
We must keep her closely monitored.

105
00:10:19,940 --> 00:10:21,897
It’s been four days, doctor.

106
00:10:27,737 --> 00:10:28,497
Prim!

107
00:10:28,828 --> 00:10:29,500
Prim!

108
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:31,137
-Ma’am, please step back.
-Prim, dear.

109
00:10:31,176 --> 00:10:31,900
Prim!

110
00:10:32,188 --> 00:10:33,939
Please wait outside, ma’am.

111
00:10:34,222 --> 00:10:34,812
Patient!

112
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:35,897
-Patient!
-Prim!

113
00:10:35,931 --> 00:10:36,700
Patient!

114
00:10:36,932 --> 00:10:37,619
Patient!

115
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:52,920
(I am a man of my word.)

116
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:08,850
THUN: I AM A MAN OF MY WORD.

117
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:21,690
PHAT: CAN WE MEET?
I HAVE TO TALK TO YOU ABOUT SOMETHING.

118
00:12:31,488 --> 00:12:32,200
Sir.

119
00:12:32,540 --> 00:12:34,595
Our target is on the move
and we’re right behind him.

120
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:41,396
How is Praew, Phat?

121
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:44,803
I heard from the doctors
that she’s conscious now.

122
00:12:45,385 --> 00:12:46,899
Physically, she’s doing better.

123
00:12:47,524 --> 00:12:49,000
But ever since she woke up,

124
00:12:49,610 --> 00:12:50,982
all she does is stare into the distance.

125
00:12:51,022 --> 00:12:53,601
She doesn’t talk
and doesn’t look at anyone.

126
00:12:56,670 --> 00:12:59,090
I cleared up with the committee
about your behavior.

127
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:01,182
You can come back to work
whenever you’re ready.

128
00:13:04,435 --> 00:13:05,203
Then…

129
00:13:06,857 --> 00:13:09,299
Can I get reassigned on the Nekros case?

130
00:13:13,450 --> 00:13:14,696
As a leader,

131
00:13:15,025 --> 00:13:17,210
I don’t think turning back on my own words
would be a good look on me.

132
00:13:18,467 --> 00:13:19,617
But don’t worry, Phat.

133
00:13:20,334 --> 00:13:23,804
I’m sure a guy like Kitti knows
what he’s doing.

134
00:13:25,902 --> 00:13:29,897
Right now there’s something
more important I need your help with.

135
00:13:33,302 --> 00:13:35,702
In the next restructuring,

136
00:13:36,004 --> 00:13:39,400
my name is on the list to be appointed
the new Commissioner-General.

137
00:13:42,424 --> 00:13:45,730
Please let me know
if you need my help with anything.

138
00:13:46,744 --> 00:13:51,803
I really believe you’ll improve our image
when you’re in office.

139
00:13:52,315 --> 00:13:56,798
That is why I have to be extra careful
not to be involved with any misconduct.

140
00:13:57,548 --> 00:13:58,499
Do you understand, Phat?

141
00:13:59,283 --> 00:14:00,100
Yes, sir.

142
00:14:02,824 --> 00:14:05,497
If you’ll excuse me…

143
00:14:06,537 --> 00:14:07,596
Thanks.

144
00:14:08,116 --> 00:14:11,200
Let me know
when Praew is out of the hospital.

145
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:12,604
Of course.

146
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:30,203
(Can we meet?
I have to talk to you about something.)

147
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:40,700
Follow me.

148
00:14:45,326 --> 00:14:46,200
What happened?

149
00:14:47,683 --> 00:14:51,250
I’m not sure about this but I feel like
I’ve been followed all morning.

150
00:14:51,489 --> 00:14:53,297
I don’t know if they’re still trailing me.

151
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:54,803
But…

152
00:14:57,712 --> 00:14:58,499
Here.

153
00:15:00,148 --> 00:15:01,896
I got all chapters of Nekros.

154
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:07,595
Where did you get them?

155
00:15:11,438 --> 00:15:13,297
I got them from Thun, the journalist.

156
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:16,850
He’s a former Nekros fan.

157
00:15:17,150 --> 00:15:18,502
He downloaded all the chapters.

158
00:15:20,022 --> 00:15:20,817
But Phat,

159
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:24,304
do you remember telling me
about how all the victims…

160
00:15:24,580 --> 00:15:26,930
were somehow involved with
the Thai Investment Bank case?

161
00:15:29,340 --> 00:15:30,203
Look.

162
00:15:30,979 --> 00:15:33,299
This is Nekros’ victim in Chapter 25.

163
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:36,796
He’s the last victim
whose information I got from Asura.

164
00:15:44,113 --> 00:15:45,890
I’m not responsible for this case anymore.

165
00:15:48,974 --> 00:15:51,996
I’ll have the investigation team
retrieve this information from you.

166
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:10,097
Follow him.

167
00:16:28,945 --> 00:16:32,610
I can guarantee Kaye
has nothing to do with the murderer.

168
00:16:35,740 --> 00:16:38,097
And I’ve got all the rest
of the chapters of Nekros.

169
00:16:40,190 --> 00:16:43,801
This is the information
on the victim in Chapter 25.

170
00:16:50,190 --> 00:16:51,702
You should focus on
catching the real murderer,

171
00:16:52,972 --> 00:16:54,400
and leave Kaye alone.

172
00:16:57,857 --> 00:17:02,198
Did you know how Kaye was involved in
the Thai Investment Bank case?

173
00:17:02,620 --> 00:17:04,600
Did you know what happened to his family?

174
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:08,400
You can’t deny the fact…

175
00:17:09,385 --> 00:17:14,499
that Kaye has motivation
to take revenge on the victims.

176
00:17:16,220 --> 00:17:20,977
And there’s a possibility
that Kaye is in fact a mastermind

177
00:17:21,020 --> 00:17:24,198
pulling the strings on his followers.

178
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,145
You know I can’t help but think that you,

179
00:17:26,180 --> 00:17:29,000
the son of the man
for whom his grudge must be the biggest,

180
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:31,097
might be one of the pawns
he’s manipulating,

181
00:17:31,542 --> 00:17:33,097
without you realizing it.

182
00:17:35,510 --> 00:17:37,601
Please don’t forget
that possibility, Inspector.

183
00:19:18,776 --> 00:19:19,504
Dad?

184
00:19:22,342 --> 00:19:24,502
Let me ask you something.

185
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:34,500
Putting up with this life

186
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:38,300
and working hard to pay for my treatment

187
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:42,297
to keep me alive today,

188
00:19:42,588 --> 00:19:46,370
are you doing it because
you love me or because you hate me?

189
00:19:51,330 --> 00:19:52,336
No, no, no.

190
00:19:52,379 --> 00:19:53,170
No, Dad.

191
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,620
You hate me.

192
00:19:55,758 --> 00:19:57,400
You hate me so much…

193
00:19:58,097 --> 00:20:00,099
you think death would be too easy for me.

194
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:01,198
No.

195
00:20:01,433 --> 00:20:02,003
No…

196
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:04,598
I’m someone who did you wrong,

197
00:20:06,260 --> 00:20:07,401
who did your mother wrong.

198
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:11,262
Am I right?

199
00:20:11,289 --> 00:20:12,504
No, no!

200
00:20:13,326 --> 00:20:16,096
That is why you’re keeping me
caged in this rotting body!

201
00:20:16,932 --> 00:20:19,100
You’re giving me hell on earth!

202
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:21,502
Why are you doing this to me?

203
00:20:21,870 --> 00:20:22,696
No…

204
00:21:15,504 --> 00:21:16,297
Hey, Nop.

205
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:19,450
(Inspector, we’ve just received
a report from Choti’s family)

206
00:21:19,610 --> 00:21:21,798
(that he’s been missing
for almost three days now.)

207
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:24,395
I’m not your boss anymore.

208
00:21:24,936 --> 00:21:26,100
(But, sir…)

209
00:21:28,024 --> 00:21:30,600
I gave all the information
to Inspector Kitti.

210
00:21:31,521 --> 00:21:32,450
(Understood, sir.)

211
00:22:17,144 --> 00:22:19,502
But they don’t even understand
everything about this case.

212
00:22:20,576 --> 00:22:21,400
Phat…

213
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:23,899
No one knows this case better than you.

214
00:22:26,064 --> 00:22:26,977
Listen to me.

215
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:31,299
You said all the victims had something
to do with the Thai Investment Bank case.

216
00:22:32,334 --> 00:22:36,300
The last jigsaw puzzle is
Choti Lertboriboon,

217
00:22:36,856 --> 00:22:39,099
the accountant who faked the accounts
for Thai Investment.

218
00:22:40,705 --> 00:22:44,739
He cooked the books
that were used in court,

219
00:22:45,352 --> 00:22:48,376
allowing all the Thai Investment Bank
executives to walk free.

220
00:22:52,947 --> 00:22:54,174
All my life,

221
00:22:55,150 --> 00:22:56,654
I never trusted anyone.

222
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:01,803
You’re the only person I trust.

223
00:23:03,740 --> 00:23:09,400
Maybe Asura is another victim
of this Thai Investment Bank case.

224
00:23:13,336 --> 00:23:14,297
Asura…

225
00:23:15,776 --> 00:23:17,001
is just like you, then?

226
00:23:23,280 --> 00:23:26,998
Inspector Kitti can be trusted, you know?

227
00:23:33,145 --> 00:23:33,897
Fine.

228
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:35,496
I get it now.

229
00:23:36,900 --> 00:23:39,700
Since everything happened because of me,

230
00:23:43,028 --> 00:23:44,996
I’ll be the one who ends it.

231
00:24:04,192 --> 00:24:05,810
(Memorials of Evil.)

232
00:24:06,496 --> 00:24:07,400
(What’s that?)

233
00:24:07,740 --> 00:24:11,580
Memorials of Evil is a name used to mark
the locations where the bodies are found

234
00:24:11,624 --> 00:24:13,170
in the Nekros manga.

235
00:24:18,960 --> 00:24:23,730
These places are well thought out
and make sense for each victim.

236
00:24:25,160 --> 00:24:26,620
CHOTI LERTBORIBOON
INVESTMENT SCAM EXPOSED

237
00:24:26,659 --> 00:24:27,730
THAI INVESTMENT BANK EXECS
TO BE INVESTIGATED FOR FRAUD

238
00:25:49,859 --> 00:25:50,696
Kaye, run.

239
00:25:50,892 --> 00:25:51,696
Run, Kaye!

240
00:26:00,659 --> 00:26:02,398
(The suspect is highly dangerous.)

241
00:26:02,977 --> 00:26:05,795
(If he shows signs of resistance,
we’ll bring him in dead.)

242
00:26:38,424 --> 00:26:39,702
He’s still here.

243
00:26:40,880 --> 00:26:41,902
Search the place.

244
00:26:42,620 --> 00:26:43,696
Don’t let him get away.

245
00:26:44,142 --> 00:26:44,976
Yes, sir.

246
00:26:45,302 --> 00:26:45,976
Let’s go.

247
00:27:26,160 --> 00:27:26,939
This room.

248
00:27:30,380 --> 00:27:31,342
This room is cleared.

249
00:27:31,379 --> 00:27:32,400
No one’s here.

250
00:27:32,577 --> 00:27:33,497
Go and check other rooms.

251
00:27:33,536 --> 00:27:34,307
Yes, sir.

252
00:29:03,772 --> 00:29:04,497
Kaye.

253
00:29:05,764 --> 00:29:06,699
Kaye, look at me.

254
00:29:06,856 --> 00:29:07,598
Kaye.

255
00:29:09,115 --> 00:29:10,656
Kaye, look at me.

256
00:29:11,377 --> 00:29:12,400
You’re safe now.

257
00:29:12,827 --> 00:29:13,860
We’re at my place.

258
00:29:16,139 --> 00:29:17,017
Calm down.

259
00:29:26,964 --> 00:29:28,003
Listen to me.

260
00:29:28,939 --> 00:29:32,930
I knew from the scene of the crime
that it wasn’t Nekros’ doing.

261
00:29:34,020 --> 00:29:37,730
He set you up to take the blame
as the serial killer.

262
00:29:39,113 --> 00:29:43,097
He’s writing the last scene with you
as the scapegoat.

263
00:29:46,702 --> 00:29:48,704
Right now, you have to get it together.

264
00:29:49,262 --> 00:29:52,299
Remember what you were doing there.

265
00:29:52,777 --> 00:29:54,201
Tell me in chronological order.

266
00:30:02,734 --> 00:30:04,102
Shit. Shit.

267
00:30:04,547 --> 00:30:05,296
I…

268
00:30:06,504 --> 00:30:08,100
I don’t remember anything.

269
00:30:09,020 --> 00:30:10,100
Not at all.

270
00:30:10,779 --> 00:30:11,902
It’s okay.

271
00:30:13,428 --> 00:30:14,896
You don’t have to remember it now.

272
00:30:17,900 --> 00:30:20,454
You can lay low here for a while.

273
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:39,099
You should clean up and get changed.

274
00:31:18,280 --> 00:31:19,136
Take these.

275
00:31:27,481 --> 00:31:29,203
I have to hurry back to investigate this.

276
00:31:31,697 --> 00:31:32,897
If I was gone too long,

277
00:31:34,193 --> 00:31:36,290
some cops might come looking around here.

278
00:31:39,736 --> 00:31:40,865
But I’ll be right back.

279
00:31:42,016 --> 00:31:42,801
Yeah.

280
00:31:43,460 --> 00:31:46,099
Just… be careful.

281
00:31:50,313 --> 00:31:51,577
I’ll keep this place locked.

282
00:31:52,566 --> 00:31:54,504
Don’t open the door for anyone but me.

283
00:31:56,763 --> 00:31:57,500
Hmm.

284
00:32:00,896 --> 00:32:01,699
Take some rest.

285
00:32:05,387 --> 00:32:08,696
I’ll find out who is behind this.

286
00:32:58,102 --> 00:32:59,699
This looks like a set up.

287
00:33:03,600 --> 00:33:06,000
Don’t you feel that it’s too easy?

288
00:33:07,059 --> 00:33:08,410
Everything just falls into place.

289
00:33:08,808 --> 00:33:10,100
I don’t “feel” it.

290
00:33:11,020 --> 00:33:12,198
I follow the evidence.

291
00:33:13,190 --> 00:33:15,699
And Kaye’s fingerprints
and the murder weapon

292
00:33:16,060 --> 00:33:17,776
are found in the crime scene.

293
00:33:24,019 --> 00:33:25,700
CHANKACHA’S HAIR IN THE CRIME SCENE

294
00:33:25,740 --> 00:33:27,099
NO. 1 SUSPECT
“KAYE”

295
00:33:27,137 --> 00:33:30,300
In all the cases before,
the murderer never left his prints

296
00:33:30,931 --> 00:33:32,500
or any evidence.

297
00:33:33,435 --> 00:33:35,697
I showed up at the scene very quickly.

298
00:33:36,020 --> 00:33:37,198
He could have slipped up.

299
00:33:37,857 --> 00:33:39,330
Stop protecting the murderer.

300
00:33:39,710 --> 00:33:41,256
I’m not protecting the murderer.

301
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:43,598
I’m protecting what is right.

302
00:33:46,064 --> 00:33:47,380
“What is right”?

303
00:33:48,598 --> 00:33:50,896
You should listen to your uncle’s advice.

304
00:33:51,490 --> 00:33:52,770
Don’t be too smart.

305
00:33:53,750 --> 00:33:55,896
Because one misstep,
and you’ll lose your footing.

306
00:33:56,096 --> 00:33:57,201
Just like your dad did.

307
00:34:01,140 --> 00:34:02,376
Keep my father out of this.

308
00:34:02,531 --> 00:34:03,297
Inspector.

309
00:34:04,290 --> 00:34:05,096
Calm down, sir.

310
00:34:12,275 --> 00:34:13,601
For your uncle’s sake,

311
00:34:14,310 --> 00:34:16,699
I won’t hold it against you
for interfering with this investigation.

312
00:34:17,616 --> 00:34:18,700
Please, Inspector.

313
00:34:19,734 --> 00:34:20,846
I’d love to get back to work.

314
00:34:39,502 --> 00:34:41,500
Keep your eye on him.

315
00:34:42,740 --> 00:34:43,810
Don’t let him out of our sight.

316
00:34:44,268 --> 00:34:44,934
Yes, sir.

317
00:34:59,480 --> 00:35:01,730
MR. KILL IDENTITY REVEALED,
THE MAN BEHIND NEKROS

318
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:04,302
That’s perfect.

319
00:35:10,145 --> 00:35:12,000
(I have to go.)

320
00:35:34,296 --> 00:35:36,699
Actually… I agree.

321
00:35:38,614 --> 00:35:40,004
I’ll give you an interview.

322
00:35:41,540 --> 00:35:42,801
Shall we begin?

323
00:35:44,777 --> 00:35:47,899
I promise to keep your face hidden

324
00:35:48,563 --> 00:35:50,450
and I’ll do all the editing myself.

325
00:35:51,344 --> 00:35:53,500
No one will get to see your face.

326
00:35:55,166 --> 00:35:56,210
Are you ready?

327
00:35:57,939 --> 00:35:58,804
Yes.

328
00:36:01,609 --> 00:36:02,376
Okay.

329
00:36:02,881 --> 00:36:05,380
We have with us here today
the creator of the manga

330
00:36:05,419 --> 00:36:07,998
that sets the world on fire.

331
00:36:08,550 --> 00:36:12,603
The manga that is the blueprint
for the vigilante murderer

332
00:36:12,820 --> 00:36:16,100
who’s dealing with the people
the laws can’t touch.

333
00:36:16,890 --> 00:36:19,696
Sitting with me here is Mr. Kill,

334
00:36:20,428 --> 00:36:22,377
the creator of Nekros.

335
00:36:23,281 --> 00:36:25,894
My first question is…

336
00:36:26,980 --> 00:36:30,102
What was the inspiration for your manga?

337
00:36:32,752 --> 00:36:40,097
The Nekros manga was inspired
by the Thai Investment Bank case.

338
00:36:41,899 --> 00:36:42,944
Did you get all the documents?

339
00:36:42,971 --> 00:36:43,619
Yes, sir.

340
00:36:43,739 --> 00:36:44,817
Don’t make any mistakes.

341
00:36:45,057 --> 00:36:46,504
This will affect how the case turns out.

342
00:36:46,540 --> 00:36:47,496
Yes, Inspector.

343
00:37:01,411 --> 00:37:06,382
My father was just a pawn
for the Thai Investment Bank.

344
00:37:06,937 --> 00:37:09,401
He ended up being their scapegoat,

345
00:37:10,824 --> 00:37:12,896
taking the blame for all the executives.

346
00:37:15,176 --> 00:37:16,296
In this world,

347
00:37:17,700 --> 00:37:20,817
justice has a cost.

348
00:37:21,730 --> 00:37:23,096
My family…

349
00:37:25,050 --> 00:37:26,576
We couldn’t afford it.

350
00:37:26,905 --> 00:37:29,420
(The court has dismissed
the top management executives)

351
00:37:29,454 --> 00:37:32,500
(in the Thai Investment Bank fraud case.)

352
00:37:32,584 --> 00:37:34,539
(All suspects are proven innocent.)

353
00:37:34,580 --> 00:37:37,782
(Another committee was set up
to investigate operational employees)

354
00:37:37,822 --> 00:37:40,530
(for involvement with faking accounts.)

355
00:37:42,250 --> 00:37:43,010
I didn’t do it!

356
00:37:43,340 --> 00:37:45,502
(The laws require someone
to take responsibility.)

357
00:37:45,870 --> 00:37:52,020
(And who’s a better scapegoat than
a nobody without a voice?)

358
00:37:52,443 --> 00:37:53,604
I’m being framed!

359
00:37:55,016 --> 00:37:56,401
I didn’t do it!

360
00:37:59,600 --> 00:38:02,450
WE ARE SCAPEGOATS.
PLEASE GIVE US JUSTICE.

361
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:04,299
GIVE ME BACK MY MONEY
SCUM FAMILY

362
00:38:04,380 --> 00:38:06,137
(The home that used to be my sanctuary)

363
00:38:06,937 --> 00:38:08,304
(became a kind of Hell)

364
00:38:10,070 --> 00:38:11,598
(that we had to put up with.)

365
00:38:13,316 --> 00:38:16,100
(And our voices were too small
for the world to hear.)

366
00:38:23,974 --> 00:38:24,740
Come on.

367
00:38:47,977 --> 00:38:48,940
-Here it is.
-Dad.

368
00:39:02,564 --> 00:39:04,195
(I still remember that day.)

369
00:39:05,875 --> 00:39:08,401
(It was the first time in months)

370
00:39:10,316 --> 00:39:12,204
(that I saw my parents smile.)

371
00:39:18,360 --> 00:39:20,604
(The taste of that meal…)

372
00:39:22,102 --> 00:39:24,600
(was the most delicious I ever tasted.)

373
00:39:25,460 --> 00:39:27,100
(But at eight years old,)

374
00:39:28,104 --> 00:39:30,001
(I was too stupid to understand)

375
00:39:31,390 --> 00:39:36,096
(that those smiles didn’t come from joy.)

376
00:39:36,614 --> 00:39:41,680
(Those were the smiles of someone
who gave up on everything.)

377
00:40:27,580 --> 00:40:29,300
(What my parents did,)

378
00:40:30,900 --> 00:40:33,004
(they didn’t do it out of hate.)

379
00:40:35,969 --> 00:40:37,396
(They did it out of love.)

380
00:40:39,499 --> 00:40:40,216
Dad!

381
00:40:41,382 --> 00:40:42,180
Mom!

382
00:40:43,140 --> 00:40:47,897
(They loved me so much they didn’t want me
to wake up in a shitty world like ours.)

383
00:40:48,500 --> 00:40:49,730
Help me!

384
00:40:49,984 --> 00:40:50,896
Dad!

385
00:40:51,156 --> 00:40:52,896
Mom!

386
00:40:53,988 --> 00:40:59,504
(The fire that day
burned my family to the ground.)

387
00:41:00,659 --> 00:41:02,702
(But there was one thing it left behind:)

388
00:41:03,416 --> 00:41:07,099
(a monster called Nekros.)

389
00:41:11,740 --> 00:41:13,297
(For me…)

390
00:41:14,393 --> 00:41:16,100
Nekros isn’t just art.

391
00:41:17,020 --> 00:41:18,780
Nekros is a symbol.

392
00:41:21,619 --> 00:41:24,497
A voice for the voiceless people.

393
00:41:27,060 --> 00:41:30,003
It was the only thing
I could do at the time

394
00:41:32,934 --> 00:41:36,419
as a response to this twisted world.

395
00:41:40,134 --> 00:41:42,897
If you thought this was a fight,

396
00:41:43,660 --> 00:41:45,697
why did you stop writing Nekros?

397
00:41:49,713 --> 00:41:53,650
Was it because you accepted your fate,

398
00:41:55,560 --> 00:41:57,499
accepted the truth,

399
00:41:58,590 --> 00:42:03,697
or the fact that your family
deserved that punishment?

400
00:42:08,300 --> 00:42:09,360
I’ll tell you what…

401
00:42:09,627 --> 00:42:12,000
As a fan of yours,

402
00:42:12,961 --> 00:42:15,795
I’d love to see you write Nekros again.

403
00:42:51,690 --> 00:42:52,464
Phat.

404
00:42:52,982 --> 00:42:54,796
I’ve been thinking about it all day.

405
00:42:56,155 --> 00:42:57,403
But I can’t think of anything.

406
00:42:58,830 --> 00:43:00,137
I can’t remember anything.

407
00:43:00,934 --> 00:43:03,096
I don’t even know how I ended up there.

408
00:43:41,670 --> 00:43:42,777
Did I kill them?

409
00:43:45,050 --> 00:43:46,462
Am I a murderer?

410
00:43:50,315 --> 00:43:51,817
Am I Nekros, Phat?

411
00:43:55,128 --> 00:43:56,702
Did I kill those people, Phat?

412
00:44:02,348 --> 00:44:03,096
Kaye.

413
00:44:05,944 --> 00:44:07,099
Listen to me.

414
00:44:09,582 --> 00:44:11,250
You helped me solve those murders.

415
00:44:12,704 --> 00:44:13,806
You helped me save people.

416
00:44:15,470 --> 00:44:16,603
You’re just a manga artist,

417
00:44:17,380 --> 00:44:18,490
writing your pain down.

418
00:44:19,220 --> 00:44:20,700
You didn’t mean for it to kill anyone.

419
00:44:23,080 --> 00:44:24,380
You’re not a murderer.

420
00:44:58,460 --> 00:44:59,216
Kaye.

421
00:45:00,420 --> 00:45:01,200
Kaye.

422
00:45:02,414 --> 00:45:03,603
Get it together, Kaye.

423
00:45:03,676 --> 00:45:04,502
Kaye.

424
00:45:04,860 --> 00:45:05,702
Get it together.

425
00:45:06,630 --> 00:45:07,890
Kaye, you need to get it together.

426
00:45:09,960 --> 00:45:10,777
Kaye.

427
00:45:16,540 --> 00:45:17,337
Kaye.

428
00:45:21,499 --> 00:45:24,184
If Inspector Phat insists on
taking the suspect’s side…

429
00:45:25,179 --> 00:45:25,896
Inspector?

430
00:45:26,116 --> 00:45:28,580
Then he’s obstructing our investigation.

431
00:45:28,740 --> 00:45:32,370
I’ll find evidence to prove
that you’re innocent.

432
00:45:32,696 --> 00:45:34,016
He’s a serial murderer.

433
00:45:34,497 --> 00:45:35,930
We’ll take him in dead or alive.

434
00:45:36,660 --> 00:45:37,297
Stop!

435
00:45:43,550 --> 00:45:44,401
Come with me.

436
00:45:44,668 --> 00:45:47,500
Thank you for not leaving me.

437
00:45:48,210 --> 00:45:50,800
I told you I’d help you no matter what.
